  "interpretation": [
    "Current installed stacks, not the historical Python oracle, are compared; Python vLLM0.31/Torch2.14/oneDNN3.13.4 differs from native oneDNN3.13.0. No driver/library/power/model change was made.",
    "Same input IDs and observed identical decoded output do not establish raw output-ID, logit, cache or numerical parity.",
    "Python resolves mamba cache mode to none when prefix cache is disabled; native retains its compact align ownership. Python allocates228/201 GPU blocks versus native requested180. Both use/request1600-token attention pages, no request was preempted.",
    "Warm medians use last3 of4 timed requests after a separate32-token primer. logprobs=0 is requested in both stacks. Cold measurements include first-use/JIT effects and remain separate.",
    "One math prompt,256 forced output tokens,greedy ignore_eos,serial C1 and three warm repetitions per arm are a narrow serving comparison; no confidence interval or larger-context/mixed/image throughput generalization.",
    "MTP public counters span all4 timed requests and may include terminal proposals beyond the public output quota.",
    "Both prefill and decode contribute materially to the MTP3 end-to-end gap. Similar/higher native proposal acceptance does not explain this gap; phase/kernel attribution needs a separately scoped profile.",
    "Full numerical,stochastic,long-context and complete Python-vision-feature parity remain open. Existing failed gates are not replaced by these timing results."
  ],
